# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# /i/<token> and /reset are single pages that read the rest of the URL in JS, so
# every path under them has to reach the same file with a 200 rather than a
# redirect. A 301 here would also break the association file's path matching.
#
# The target is the directory, NOT <dir>/index.html. Cloudflare canonicalises an
# asset stored at i/index.html to the path /i/, and a rewrite aimed at the
# uncanonical /i/index.html can fail to resolve and fall through to not-found
# handling, which is what shipped in a5b4fdd. See README.md.
/i/*      /i/      200
/reset/*  /reset/  200
